      "answer_text": "`hermes-all-three` is the package to use. It is one composed `ContextEngine` that applies A, B and D together in a single `select_context`, `get_tool_schemas` and `on_turn_complete`.\n\nSeparate plugins can't run at once because Hermes allows only one active context engine. `PluginRegistration.register_context_engine` at `hermes_cli/plugins.py:717` refuses a second one. The check is `if self._manager._context_engine is not None: logger.warning(...); return`. The second engine is not registered, and the only trace is a logged warning. You choose the engine with `context.engine: <name>` in `config.yaml`.\n\nBoth points are from `hermes-plugins/CONTRACT.md` (§3) and the `hermes-plugins/README.md` section \"Why four packages — Hermes is single-select\", which I read earlier. I haven't re-read them or checked that line number against the Hermes source."
    },
