      "answer_text": "The OpenCode plugin sends a heartbeat every 120,000 ms (120 s). That is `HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 120_000` at `.opencode/plugins/context-engineering.ts:138`, used by the `setInterval` at line 185.\n\n**Why it's needed:**\n- **The lease:** the bridge keeps each session's stored originals under a memory-only retention lease. The comment at line 137 says the lease needs a sign of life within 300 s, and 120 s renews it well inside that window.\n- **What expires:** per the README, without any sign of life the lease lapses after 300 s and the stored reference expires after another 300 s.\n- **Why it matters:** a model can call `retrieve_context` many turns and minutes after a preview was made. Without the heartbeat, the original could be gone by then and the retrieval would be refused.\n- **Who gets it:** every session the plugin has seen, tracked in `liveSessions`. It is dropped on `session.deleted`.\n- **Other renewals:** any request for a session also renews its lease. The heartbeat covers the quiet stretches when no tool calls or retrievals happen."
    },
